# Line-ending policy.
#
# The project explicitly supports checking the repo out on Windows (the bridge
# is built with a native cargo.exe). A Windows `git clone` defaults to
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which would rewrite `bootstrap.sh` and `pam-config` to
# CRLF and break them: the installer's shebang and the PAM profile parser both
# expect LF. Force LF for tracked text files regardless of the local setting.
#
# Rules are evaluated in order, last match wins, so the explicit `pam-config`
# rule below re-asserts LF against `* text=auto` and binary files are opted out.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
pam-config text eol=lf

# Binaries must never be line-ending-normalized.
*.exe binary
*.so binary
